            "items": [
              {
                "text": "## Birch Ownership and Pending Handoff Items\n\n### Who Owns Birch\n\n**Rhea Vale owns the Birch service.** This is consistently documented across multiple independent records and decision logs, confirming it as an established fact rather than a passing mention:\n\n- Cited in the deployment handoff review documentation\n- Repeated as a formal \"decision: Hindsight interruption source\" entry\n- Recorded multiple times with distinct timestamps (2026-09-07 at 16:43 and again at 17:35)\n\nThe repeated confirmation across separate entries strengthens the reliability of this ownership fact.\n\n### What Remains Pending in the Reviewed Birch Deployment Handoff\n\nThe reviewed deployment handoff (reference **7bcf906b-c524-457e-845a-e6c297638cee**) contains the following key status:\n\n- **The deployment checklist review remains pending.** The Birch transfer cannot be formally closed until this review is completed.\n\nThe handoff notes structure the remaining work as follows:\n\n| Item | Status |\n|------|--------|\n| Birch service ownership | Confirmed \u2014 Rhea Vale |\n| Deployment checklist review | **Pending** (blocks transfer close) |\n| Birch transfer closure | Blocked until checklist is reviewed |\n\n### Next Step Identified in the Handoff\n\nThe handoff explicitly lists a single next step:\n\n> Review the deployment checklist before closing the Birch transfer.\n\nThere are no additional open questions detailed in the available records, meaning the checklist review is the sole outstanding item standing between the current state and a closed Birch transfer.\n\n### Summary\n\n**Rhea Vale owns the Birch service**, and the one remaining item in the reviewed deployment handoff is the **deployment checklist review**, which must be completed before the Birch transfer can be closed.",
